# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0) so GitHub renders a
# "Cite this repository" button and downstream research can reference the
# software precisely. Bump `version` and `date-released` in lockstep with
# the release checklist in RELEASING.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "BirdNet-Behavior"
abstract: >-
  Real-time acoustic bird classification with DuckDB behavioral analytics.
  A ground-up Rust rewrite of BirdNET-Pi that runs the BirdNET+ neural
  network on a Raspberry Pi or x86_64 Linux host as a single self-contained
  binary, with sessionization, retention, funnel, and sequence analytics
  over detected bird activity. BirdNET is developed by the K. Lisa Yang
  Center for Conservation Bioacoustics at the Cornell Lab of Ornithology
  and Chemnitz University of Technology.
authors:
  - alias: tomtom215
    family-names: "F."
    given-names: Tom
repository-code: "https://github.com/tomtom215/BirdNet-Behavior"
url: "https://tomtom215.github.io/BirdNet-Behavior/"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
version: 0.7.2
date-released: "2026-06-07"
keywords:
  - birdnet
  - bioacoustics
  - bird-classification
  - acoustic-monitoring
  - duckdb
  - raspberry-pi
  - rust
references:
